  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn coin. Then the support is $S={5,10,25}.$\n\nIn the bag there are $2$ nickels, $4$ dimes, and $4$ quarters (ten coins in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{4}{10}=\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ P(25) & =\\frac{4}{10}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+25\\cdot f(25) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{1}{5})+10(\\frac{2}{5})+25(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5}+\\frac{20}{5}+\\frac{50}{5} \\\\  & =1+4+10 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
